# Copy to /etc/igor/env (systemd) or .env (compose). Contains credentials: chmod 600.
#
# Seat tokens belong here, because a seat is a subscription several Igors may draw from.
# GH_TOKEN does not, once more than one Igor runs on the machine: put it in a per-instance
# file, /etc/igor/<role>.env, or every Igor claims as the same account.

# One per seat, named by `token_env` in igor.config.yaml. From `claude setup-token` run
# while signed in as that seat. A seat naming a variable that is unset is skipped, never
# substituted with whatever login is ambient.
IGOR_SEAT_1=

# --- /etc/igor/<role>.env, one per Igor ---

# Who this Igor is on the tracker and the code host. `gh` reads it, and Igor shells out to
# `gh`, so this variable is the identity: a fine-grained token for this Igor's machine
# account, scoped to the repositories it works, with Issues, Pull requests and Contents
# read/write. Not admin, not a classic token. See docs/machine-accounts.md.
GH_TOKEN=
